Krater is an interesting and original RPG, with a clear action orientation and an unusual post-apocalyptic universe that pulls you in quite easily.
However, I had much issues with a key design choice made by the developers: in Krater, instead of leveling up one or several heroes over time like you would do in Diablo or Torchlight, your heroes quickly reach a maximum level. This is the game's way to encourage you to level up many different characters, try out new tactics, etc. But for me, it was a blocker: I didn't want to be "forced" to level up different heroes, I wanted to keep improving the ones I loved, but that wasn't possible.
For this reason, past the first few hours of honeymoon with the game, I found it had lost most of its charm, and became quite repetitive, as I had lost this "drive". For this reason, I wouldn't necessarily recommend Krater, despite it being quite original and with an great quirky setting;
